  "relation": "observation",
  "args": "{\"description\":\"PERF: logue felt ~1.3s/keypress because draw() repainted all 60x18=1080 cells every frame. Measured headless (zig-out birnam): tileAt over one full map = 1023ms (1080 calls ~0.95ms each, dominated by re-reading the [tiles value] CELL deref ~0.15ms + a HAMT map at:ifAbsent: lookup, per cell), and tb setCell x1080 = 273ms (~0.25ms per libffi keyword-send). Two general birnam lessons: (1) a 'db cell:' value read is ~150us (currentValue+dispatch), NOT the ~20ns raw field read — HOIST cell reads out of inner loops. (2) each wrapped FFI keyword-send is ~250us, so minimize FFI call COUNT in hot paths. Fix: static-map-once + dirty-cell repaint (player+monsters+items only, ~40 FFI calls/frame). A full per-frame redraw of a screenful of cells is not viable at birnam interp speed.\",\"kind\":\"antipattern\",\"scope\":\"birnam:examples/logue\",\"source\":\"chazu\",\"status\":\"raw\",\"worth\":0.5}",
