  "relation": "observation",
  "args": "{\"description\":\"Birnam hard limit: block value: dispatch supports at most 4 arguments. A 5+ parameter block '[:a :b :c :d :e | ...]' called '[blk value: ... value: ...]' (5x) raises 'does not understand: #value:value:value:value:value:'. value/value:/value:value:/value:value:value:/value:value:value:value: exist; 5-ary and up do not. Forces grouping args into a map/vector for any function needing 5+ params (refactored carveRoom(tmap,rx,ry,rw,rh) and stockRoom(7 args) to take a room-map). Worth a clearer error than generic doesNotUnderstand, and/or a variadic valueWithArguments: (vector) entry point.\",\"kind\":\"obstacle\",\"scope\":\"birnam:examples/logue\",\"source\":\"chazu\",\"status\":\"raw\",\"worth\":0.5}",
