{
  "id": "de35c528b2a5fc3c3bd0dee3c8d168d391d598fbc26d0a693a122a60885cce61",
  "relation": "observation",
  "args": "{\"description\":\"Birnam's batch file-in (lang fileIn:/:in/:in!) reports only an aggregate 'filed in N forms (M errors)' count to stderr — it does NOT print which forms failed or why when M\\u003e0 and the in is non-atomic. (A PARSE error triggers atomic abort and DOES echo the offending form; but per-form EVAL/compile errors are silently counted and skipped, leaving their globals unbound.) This makes debugging a multi-form script painful: you see '4 errors' with no location. Worked around by probing each global with a caught error. Suggestion: fileIn should emit 'error at form N (line L): \\u003creason\\u003e' per failed form, as the atomic path already does.\",\"kind\":\"suggestion\",\"scope\":\"birnam:examples/logue\",\"source\":\"chazu\",\"status\":\"raw\",\"worth\":0.5}",
  "valid_start": 1782261635,
