  "args": "{\"description\":\"termbox2 default TB_OPT_ATTR_W=64, so tb_set_cell/tb_print take uintattr_t fg/bg as uint64_t (not uint16). Confirms the int-clean C adapter is REQUIRED, not just convenient: a birnam SmallInt passed directly to a wrapped uint64 param via libffi sigchar 'i' (sint32) would mismatch the ABI. The lg_* adapter takes int and casts to uintattr_t, isolating the width. General lesson: prefer a thin int/pointer-clean C adapter over a single-header lib rather than wrapping its real signatures when the lib uses width-configurable typedefs.\",\"kind\":\"pattern\",\"scope\":\"birnam:examples/logue\",\"source\":\"chazu\",\"status\":\"raw\",\"worth\":0.5}",
